{"book":"PSA","chapter":100,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4,5],"records":[{"id":"PSA.100.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"מִזְמ֥וֹר לְתוֹדָ֑ההָרִ֥יעוּ לַ֝יהוָ֗ה כָּל־הָאָֽרֶץ׃","gloss":"A psalm for thanksgiving. Shout to YHWH, all the earth.","pieces":[[1,"A psalm for giving thanks. \\q Raise a glad shout to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, all the earth!",null]],"L":{"1":"A psalm for thanksgiving. \\q Shout for joy to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, all the earth."},"R":{"1":"A song for giving thanks. \\q Everyone on earth, shout to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} with joy!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o191000010011","o191000010021","o191000010022"],"choice":"The title shares verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"This psalm's title is short and the Hebrew counts it together with the first line as verse 1, so here the verse numbers are the same as in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000010022"],"choice":"for thanksgiving: for giving thanks","alternatives":["for the thank offering"],"reason":"The word (todah) is thanks, and also the thank offering (Leviticus 7:12). The psalm may have been sung when such an offering was brought; verse 4 has worshipers entering the temple gates with thanks.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000010031"],"choice":"shout: the cry that greets a king","alternatives":[],"reason":"The same verb (heria') as 98:4 and 95:1: the glad shout raised for the King.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"All the earth, come in with thanks","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.100.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"עִבְד֣וּ אֶת־יְהוָ֣ה בְּשִׂמְחָ֑ה בֹּ֥אוּ לְ֝פָנָ֗יו בִּרְנָנָֽה׃","gloss":"Serve YHWH with gladness; come before him with a joyful cry.","pieces":[[2,"Serve {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} and be glad doing it; \\q come before {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} with ringing cries of joy.",null]],"L":{"2":"Serve {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} with gladness; \\q come before {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} with joyful singing."},"R":{"2":"Be happy as you serve {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}! \\q Come to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} singing for joy!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000020011"],"choice":"serve: work for and worship","alternatives":["worship"],"reason":"The verb ('avad) is the work a servant does for a master or subjects for a king, and also worship (Exodus 3:12). All the earth is called to serve the LORD as King.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000020072"],"choice":"a joyful cry: a ringing shout or song","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (renanah) is a loud cry of joy.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.100.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"דְּע֗וּ כִּֽי־יְהוָה֮ ה֤וּא אֱלֹ֫הִ֥ים הֽוּא־עָ֭שָׂנוּ וְל֣וֹ אֲנַ֑חְנוּ עַ֝מּ֗וֹ וְצֹ֣אן מַרְעִיתֽוֹ׃","gloss":"Know that YHWH, he [is] God; he made us, and his [are] we, his people and [the] flock of his pasture.","pieces":[[3,"Be sure of this: {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} is God! \\q He is the one who made us, and we belong to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}. \\q We are {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} people, the flock {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} pastures.",null]],"L":{"3":"Know that {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} [is] God! \\q It [is] {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} [who] made us, and {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} [are] we, \\q {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} people and the flock of {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} pasture."},"R":{"3":"You must understand that {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} is the true God. \\q He made us, and we belong to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}. \\q We are {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} people. We are like sheep, and {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} cares for us like a shepherd."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"text_variant","tokens":["o191000030091","o191000030092","o191000030093"],"choice":"and we are his: the words as read, not as written","alternatives":["and not we ourselves (as written)"],"reason":"The Hebrew text writes \"and not (lo') we\" and its notes say to read \"and his (lo) we [are]\"; the two sound alike. The written form gives \"he made us, and not we ourselves\", which the ancient Greek translation follows. The form to be read fits the next words, \"his people and the flock of his pasture\", and the words here follow it.","uncertain":false,"footnote":true},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000030011"],"choice":"know: acknowledge, be sure","alternatives":[],"reason":"To know here is to recognize and confess (46:11), not only to have heard.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191000030122","o191000030131"],"choice":"the flock of his pasture: the people he shepherds","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 95:7 and 79:13, God's people are his flock and he is their shepherd.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191000030051"],"choice":"the true God","alternatives":["God"],"reason":"Readable brings out the emphasis of \"the LORD, he is God\" (1 Kings 18:39).","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191000030122","o191000030131"],"choice":"like sheep, and he cares for us like a shepherd","alternatives":["the flock of his pasture"],"reason":"Readable makes the picture a comparison (m3).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.100.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"בֹּ֤אוּ שְׁעָרָ֨יו׀בְּתוֹדָ֗ה חֲצֵרֹתָ֥יו בִּתְהִלָּ֑ה הֽוֹדוּ־ל֝֗וֹ בָּרֲכ֥וּ שְׁמֽוֹ׃","gloss":"Enter his gates with thanksgiving, his courts with praise; give thanks to him, bless his name.","pieces":[[4,"Come through {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} gates giving thanks, \\q into {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} courtyards with praise; \\q thank {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} and bless {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} name.",null]],"L":{"4":"Enter {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} gates with thanksgiving, \\q {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} courts with praise; \\q give thanks to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}, bless {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} name."},"R":{"4":"Go through the gates of {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} temple thanking {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}. \\q Go into its courtyards praising {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}. \\q Thank {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} and praise {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} name."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191000040021","o191000040041"],"choice":"gates and courts: the way into the temple","alternatives":[],"reason":"Worshipers went in through the temple gates into its open courts (24:7; 96:8).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000040032"],"choice":"thanksgiving: thanks, perhaps a thank offering","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (todah) is the same as in the title (verse 1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o191000040021"],"choice":"of his temple","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable says whose gates these are.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.100.5.s1","verses":[5],"source":"כִּי־ט֣וֹב יְ֭הֹוָה לְעוֹלָ֣ם חַסְדּ֑וֹ וְעַד־דֹּ֥ר וָ֝דֹ֗ר אֱמוּנָתֽוֹ׃","gloss":"For good [is] YHWH; forever [is] his loyal love, and to generation and generation his faithfulness.","pieces":[[5,"For {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} is good; {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} loyal love has no end, \\q and {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} faithfulness stands from one generation to the next.",null]],"L":{"5":"For good [is] {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}; forever [is] {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} loyal love, \\q and to generation and generation {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} faithfulness."},"R":{"5":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} is good! His faithful love lasts forever. \\q He keeps {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} promises to every generation, one after another."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000050051"],"choice":"loyal love: chesed","alternatives":["steadfast love","kindness","mercy"],"reason":"The word (chesed) is the love that keeps faith, God's commitment to his people that does not give up (5:8).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o191000050021","o191000050051"],"choice":"the song of the temple: good, love forever","alternatives":[],"reason":"\"Good\" and \"his loyal love is forever\" are the words of the temple's great song of thanks (106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1; 2 Chronicles 5:13).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191000050091"],"choice":"faithfulness: firm reliability","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word ('emunah) is steadiness, being someone others can rely on.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191000050051"],"choice":"faithful love","alternatives":["loyal love"],"reason":"As in the earlier psalms, Readable says \"faithful love\" for chesed.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191000050091"],"choice":"keeps his promises","alternatives":["his faithfulness"],"reason":"Readable says what God's faithfulness does.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"he